.\" Manpage for castmirror. Apache-2.0. See NOTICE for the GPL implications of
.\" distributing a binary linked against libx264.
.TH CASTMIRROR 1 "2026-09-23" "CastMirror 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
castmirror \- send a display or window to a Google Cast receiver
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B castmirror
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B castmirror
is the interactive and flag-driven command line front end to the CastMirror
core. It discovers Google Cast, Android TV and Nest receivers on the local
network, captures a display or a single window, encodes H.264 video with VAAPI
or FFmpeg libx264 and Opus audio, and streams the result over the Cast
Streaming protocol (CAST/CST2 RTP over UDP with compound RTCP).
.PP
Run with no options to enter the interactive prompt.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-device " <IP or ID>"
Target receiver by IP address or Cast device UUID. Implies non-interactive mode.
.TP
.BI \-\-display " <ID>"
Display or monitor index to capture. Default is 0.
.TP
.BI \-\-window " <ID>"
Share a single window, identified by its X11 XID. Use
.B \-\-list-windows
to enumerate IDs.
.TP
.B \-\-list-windows
List capturable windows and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-list-displays
List available displays and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-preset " <preset>"
Quality preset: Auto, High, Balanced, Smooth, Game or Cinema. Default is Auto.
Game requests a 150 ms target playout delay; Cinema requests 400 ms.
.TP
.B \-\-no-audio
Disable audio mirroring.
.TP
.BI \-\-bitrate " <kbps>"
Custom video bitrate ceiling in kilobits per second.
.TP
.BI \-\-codec " <h264|vp8>"
Select the video codec. Default is h264.
.TP
.B \-\-low-latency
Force a 200 ms target playout delay.
.TP
.B \-\-no-verify
Bypass Cast device certificate verification. Development escape hatch; do not
use it on an untrusted network.
.TP
.BI \-\-auth-probe " <IP>"
Connect to a device, run the device authentication challenge and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show the help message and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CASTMIRROR_FORCE_SOFTWARE_ENCODE=1
Force FFmpeg libx264 software encoding even where VAAPI hardware encoding is
available.
.TP
.B CASTMIRROR_FORCE_X11=1
Force X11 capture instead of the Wayland xdg-desktop-portal ScreenCast path.
.TP
.B CASTMIRROR_CONFIG_DIR=/path/to/dir
Read and write
.I config.json
in this directory instead of the default per-user location.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/castmirror/config.json
Persisted settings.
.TP
.I ~/.config/castmirror/castmirror.log
Rotating debug log.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
castmirror \-\-device 192.168.1.150 \-\-display 0 \-\-preset High
castmirror \-\-device 192.168.1.150 \-\-no-audio
castmirror \-\-list-windows
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR castmirror-gui (1),
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR pactl (1)
.SH NOTES
Distributing a compiled CastMirror binary linked against GPL-licensed libx264
generally requires treating that binary as GPL. See the NOTICE file shipped
with the source.
